        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.59,
            0.847,
            0.648
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can see that all of them represent the number (– 2). Now, take 4 times each of these token sets. That is, place each set into the empty bag 4 times."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.657,
            0.802,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What integer do we get as the final answer in each case? Do we get different answers because the sets look different, or the same answer because they all represent – 2?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.816,
            0.655,
            0.904,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 15,
              "bbox": [
                0.816,
                0.655,
                0.904,
                0.724
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_15.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.731,
            0.81,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Check this for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 \\times 4 ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " by taking different token sets corresponding to 4."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.757,
            0.847,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have seen that – 4 × 2 is the number obtained by removing 2 positive tokens from the empty bag 4 times."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.796,
            0.846,
            0.833
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that removing or subtracting a number is the same as adding its inverse. 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.834,
            0.803,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using this, can – 4 × 2 be defined through a process of addition of tokens instead of removal of tokens?"
            }
          ]
        },
